# HEAT — sample environment. Copy to `.env` and fill in. Never commit `.env`.
#
# ⚠️ NOTHING READS THIS YET. As of 2026-07-31 the pages are static HTML served by
# GitHub Pages with no build step, so these values are hardcoded inline:
#
#   heat/assess.html:216    const FOLIO_EP = "https://<ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/heat-folio"
#   heat/success.html:50    fetch('https://<ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/heat-claim?session_id=...')
#
# A file that looks like config and is read by nobody is worse than no file, so:
# if you add a build step or a server, wire those two lines to these vars and
# delete this warning. Until then treat this as the shape, not the source.

# Supabase project the edge functions live on.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Publishable ("anon") key. Safe in a browser BY DESIGN — it is only ever as safe
# as your row-level security, so treat RLS as the actual secret.
# ⚠️ The current pages do NOT send this: heat-claim / heat-folio are deployed with
# verify_jwt=false and authenticate on the purchase key in the body instead.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_replace_me

# ⛔ SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Never in a page, never in this repo, never in a bundle.
# Bypasses row-level security entirely.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ⛔ SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Stripe webhook signing secret for the stripe-webhook function.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me
